<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleopatra Selene II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">40 BCE – c. 5 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Cleopatra Selene</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleopatra Selene II was the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, born in 40 BCE as the twin of Alexander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helios">Helios</a>. After her parents' deaths she was raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> by Octavia and around 25 BCE married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-ii">Juba II</a>, becoming queen of Mauretania. She promoted Greek and Egyptian culture at the court of Caesarea, and her son Ptolemy succeeded Juba.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cleopatra-selene-ii.jpg" alt="Cleopatra Selene II" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hichem algerino · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cleopatra_Selene_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
